   "adp_definition": "ADP is the consensus average draft position blended across public sources (Fantasy Football Calculator, MyFantasyLeague, Sleeper), weighted FFC 0.5, MFL 0.3, SLEEPER 0.2 and matched to this league's format (full-PPR; half-PPR in 2010), 12-team. It is the closest public market to this league \u2014 not its own valuations. Reach / value is the gap between where the league drafted a player and the consensus, judged against a tolerance that grows with draft depth: a pick well earlier than its ADP is a reach, well later is a value, and anything inside the depth-scaled cushion reads as on-market. The cushion is tight at the top (where the elite tier is interchangeable and ordering is preference) and widens deeper into the draft (where exact slot matters less).",
